        "id": 18620,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-09T21:10:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't play BODAN very often, so this really hasn't come up in game play, but I was reading the FAQ (<a href=\"https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.7w4g9jv\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.7w4g9jv</a>), and noticed this question/answer:</p>\n<p><strong><em>Can Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares do real damage (destroying cities, etc) with Power X?</em></strong></p>\n<div>\n\t<em>The answer, in general, is 'no'. If the Power says \"damage\" or \"destroy\", it doesn't matter if it also says that Dahan, Beasts, Invaders, or anything else are doing that damage, the source is still ultimately Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares and is only nightmare damage.</em>\n</div>\n<div>\n\t&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n\tThis doesn't make sense to me from a philosophical/flavor standpoint:&nbsp; If BODAN is (ex:) giving some Invaders some nasty dreams that cause them to turn on/attack each other, or is invading the dreams of Dahan or beasts and prompting them to attack the invaders, shouldn't that be real damage and not dream damage?</div>\n<div>\n\t&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n\t&nbsp;</div>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:02.220Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 55,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
