        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"Lorkenpeist\"]\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<div class=\"bb-quote\">\n\t<b>Ameena wrote:</b><br />\n\t<blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">\n\t\tVolcanic eruption? Tigers chewing your face off? Disease causing your skin to melt? Floodwater washing away you and your home and everyone you know and all their houses too? Nope, not really - it's all inside your head.\n\t\t\n&nbsp;\n\n\t</blockquote>\n</div>\n\nAnd yet somehow that volcanic eruption leaves actual blight on the island.\n\n[/quote]\n\nInteresting point -- if the whole thing is just a nightmare about a volcano destroying the island, how does it produce \"fictitious\" damage, but \"real\" blight?&nbsp;\n\nIt seems like you can't have it both ways -- if BODAN's powers can't do any physical damage to things, they shouldn't be able to do any physical blight, either.&nbsp; And really, they shouldn't be able to *remove* blight, either.&nbsp; A beautiful dream that the island has been cleaned up doesn't mean that the island has in fact actually *been* cleaned up.\n\nAnd what about the Dahan?&nbsp; A power like (ex:) Razor Sharp Undergrowth or Poisoned Land is supposed to destroy Dahan.&nbsp; The card says \"...nor can [your Powers] destroy anything except your own [Presence],\" which seems to indicate that those powers would not, in fact, destroy any Dahan.&nbsp; What do they in fact, do?&nbsp; The \"destroyed\" explorers/towns move elsewhere, but do the \"destroyed\" Dahan just stay where they are?&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n(Apologies, BTW, if these issues/questions have been addressed in other FAQs/threads.)\n\n&nbsp;\n",
